1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,124
The map of your company's data is probably wrong.

2
00:00:03,174 --> 00:00:05,298
Here's why, and the simple fix.

3
00:00:05,748 --> 00:00:09,273
Every app keeps information: customers, orders, payments.

4
00:00:09,323 --> 00:00:12,575
A data map shows what's kept, and how it all connects.

5
00:00:13,025 --> 00:00:16,923
For decades, that map was drawn in a separate tool, for the managers.

6
00:00:16,973 --> 00:00:19,629
The engineers build the real thing somewhere else.

7
00:00:19,679 --> 00:00:22,914
It's like keeping the blueprints in a different city to the building site.

8
00:00:22,964 --> 00:00:27,803
So the map slowly stops being true, and people make decisions on the wrong picture.

9
00:00:28,253 --> 00:00:31,688
I'm a data engineer, and I wanted AI to help build it all.

10
00:00:31,738 --> 00:00:35,027
But it could read the code, not the map. So it had to guess.

11
00:00:35,753 --> 00:00:39,499
So I moved the map right next to the code, as a simple text file.

12
00:00:39,549 --> 00:00:41,368
Now the AI reads it too.

13
00:00:42,253 --> 00:00:46,185
ERD Studio turns that file into a picture anyone can read.

14
00:00:46,235 --> 00:00:49,637
Change the picture, the file changes. And vice versa.

15
00:00:50,087 --> 00:00:52,585
And if what's really built stops matching the map,

16
00:00:52,635 --> 00:00:55,662
it lights up the difference, before it causes problems.

17
00:00:57,587 --> 00:01:00,654
Now the map and the code change together, in one approval.

18
00:01:00,704 --> 00:01:03,660
Reviewed together. Tracked together. Shipped together.

19
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:07,599
It's just common sense. Why did this take us decades to figure out?

20
00:01:08,587 --> 00:01:12,565
And managers still see the picture, right on their team's wiki page.

21
00:01:14,587 --> 00:01:16,627
And since the launch, it's taking off.

22
00:01:16,677 --> 00:01:17,947
Come and see why.

23
00:01:20,087 --> 00:01:24,318
ERD Studio for VS Code. Free, with the source on GitHub.

24
00:01:24,368 --> 00:01:27,866
Know a data team? Send them this. Link in the comments.
